<Prose
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Rounder's privacy policy. Tools run in your browser, so your files and text are never uploaded to our servers."
  heading="Privacy"
  updated="October 2026"
>
  <p><strong>Short version:</strong> the files and text you use with our tools never leave your device. We don't have accounts, so we don't hold your email, name or password.</p>

  <h2>Your files and text</h2>
  <p>
    Every tool on Rounder processes data locally in your browser. Files you drop in, text you paste and results you generate
    are not uploaded to or stored on our servers. Some AI tools download a model file the first time you use them, from
    our site or from Hugging Face, a public model library. That download only goes to you; nothing about your input goes
    the other way.
  </p>

  <h2>The few tools that go online</h2>
  <p>A handful of tools need a little data from the internet, and they say so on the page:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The <a href="/currency-converter">currency converter</a> fetches daily exchange rates from the Frankfurter API (European Central Bank reference rates). Only the request for rates is sent, never the amounts you type.</li>
    <li>The <a href="/password-strength-checker">password strength checker</a> can check whether a password appeared in a known data breach, but only if you click to do so. It then sends the first 5 characters of the password's SHA-1 hash to Have I Been Pwned, never the password itself.</li>
    <li>AI tools download their model the first time you run them, after asking you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What your browser stores</h2>
  <p>
    We keep a few small things in your browser's local storage to make the site nicer, such as your recently used tools and
    downloaded AI models. They stay on your device and you can clear them at any time in your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    To keep Rounder free we may show ads and measure basic, aggregated traffic (such as how many people visit a page). Ad
    partners may use cookies according to their own policies, and where the law requires it we will ask for your consent
    first. Ad and analytics scripts never receive your files or tool input.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@roundertools.com">hello@roundertools.com</a>.</p>
</Prose>
